# Byte pins for the manual pack /opt/strata/bin/fetch_models.sh stages
# (cf-86 C02's orcarouter rung, on the IQ4_XS tier since the U9.2 owner
# ruling), sourced by that driver.
#
# Why a sourced file instead of literals on the download legs: the legs, the
# pack contract and the test suite all need the same numbers, and the
# values.yaml heredocs kept them next to the code that used them only as long
# as the code lived in the chart. Two homes for one literal is how a shard
# pin drifts; this file is the single home (C07 lift, U9.4).
#
# Provenance: HF tree API read anonymously 2026-10-31 — lfs.size per shard,
# the exact values the staged pack is built and delivered against. hf_fetch.py
# renames a .part only on an EXACT size match, so a literal that drifts by even
# a few hundred bytes is a silently truncated shard entering iq_pack. Re-read
# the tree before touching one.

# orcarouter/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Uncensored-GGUF, IQ4_XS tier, 3 shards at the
# flat repo root (the tier ships no per-quant subdir — resolved by the live
# tree read, not assumed) — gated bytes, public metadata.
# Σ 97473155200 = RESEARCH R4 [B7]'s 97.47 GB; the MTP sibling family in the
# same tree is deliberately NOT staged (experts-only, as everywhere here).
ORCA_IQ4_XS_SHARD1=44766155936
ORCA_IQ4_XS_SHARD2=44735995008
ORCA_IQ4_XS_SHARD3=7971004256

# unsloth/Ornith-1.5-122B-GGUF, UD-Q4_K_XL tier, three shards under the tier
# directory (cf-86 C09's GGUF-direct q36 rung — the engine reads these files
# as they ship, so what is staged here is exactly what the serve profile
# points at). Public bytes: the anonymous tree read answered gated=false and a
# ranged resolve of the middle shard answered 206 with GGUF magic, so these
# legs take hf_fetch's anon mode with no token involved — the mirror image of
# the orca trio above.
# Σ 79713771665 = RESEARCH R5 [C7]'s 79.7 GB. Shard 1 is the 10.9 MB head —
# GGUF metadata + tokenizer only, its own header answers n_tensors 0 (C09
# review-r1 GGUF census), not a rounding artifact: it is unsloth's split
# boundary, which is why a plausible-looking first shard size would be wrong.
ORNITH_UD_Q4_K_XL_SHARD1=10942929
ORNITH_UD_Q4_K_XL_SHARD2=49971099680
ORNITH_UD_Q4_K_XL_SHARD3=29731729056
